  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-02-24T23:46:35.129Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Nobody* asked for it but you gave it to us anyways: https://medium.com/vrchat/upcoming-status-system-changes-ed7f824e96ff Binary status, available/joinable or not available/not-joinable. Now please revert it or refine it such that we can let friends know that we're busy or asleep but they can join us anyway if they want to do so.\nHow about turning the \"Ask me\" status into an \"Inactive\" or \"Busy\" status and allowing friends to join you while letting them know that you're there, just not very reactive right now or maybe even asleep?\n*) To be fair, 70 people asked for it in https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/busy-status-could-require-an-invite-request-to-join-on-friend and 140 people asked for it in https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/do-not-disturb-status-to-prevent-people-from-joining-on-you-directly-even-if-you and I'm not strictly against the idea of appearing as online, always showing up as private while being in a friends/friends+/public instance but a lot of concerns have been raised and the updated implementation really needs a status that just says \"I'm busy. Feel free to join me anyways but don't expect too much reaction\", you essentially didn't have to remove or change the way the \"Busy\" status works, all that we asked you to do was to *add* an option that allows us to set an invisible-like status.",
